docs/progress/R76/raw/004_prior_submission_and_quickbuild_context.txt:211:docs/hq/step0_analysis_rev6.md:262:> **Verification boundary**: these are **local GBS build** results. Build verification on QuickBuild is in progress. Also under verification is whether QuickBuild supports multiple spec files coexisting under the llvm package — if it does not, the delivery form will need to be reconsidered.
docs/progress/R76/raw/004_prior_submission_and_quickbuild_context.txt:212:docs/hq/step0_analysis_rev6.md:547:> **Incident record** (referenced from §9-2): LLVM 22.1.8 failed to build libc++abi on armv7l because upstream PR #116261 removed a declaration of `__gnu_unwind_frame` and moved it into a header belonging to LLVM's own unwind library; configurations not using that library never see it. Upstream fixed this in PR #189787 and carried it into the 22.x release milestone. We backported the upstream fix (patch content identical to upstream) and verified: build succeeds, zero warnings/errors, zero unresolved symbols, ARM exception table sections present, correct binding to `libgcc_s.so.1`. Verified on QuickBuild sandbox as having no side effects on the platform LLVM build.
docs/progress/R76/raw/004_prior_submission_and_quickbuild_context.txt:213:docs/hq/step0_analysis_rev6.md:569:   │                                      QuickBuild verification in progress
